CSS `.log-entry.fresh{animation:logIn .3s ease both}` remove animation from base. But reverse index: newest first. When log grows by several entries, only top gets fresh. Fine. On initial render, lastLogLen 0 -> first fresh, others static. Good.

But updateLog called when new game starts with log length maybe 1-2; lastLogLen from previous session might be larger. Reset lastLogLen when? Could just animate when i===0 always? That causes only top entry to re-animate on each refresh (AI flicker on top entry). Minor. Better track a monotonic log count across game changes? On new game, log length resets, lastLogLen larger -> no animation. Acceptable.

Maybe simpler: remove animation entirely. Visual quality okay without. But logIn is nice when new entries appear. Let's implement the lastLogLen approach and reset in enterGame? enterGame calls update which calls updateLog; set lastLogLen=0 at start of enterGame? But restoring game has existing log -> would animate top only. Fine.

Actually easiest: in updateLog compute new items, and set animation only when `e._new`? Not persisted.

I'll do lastLogLen. Also the turn duplicate fix.

