```
This is object literal arrow with parentheses, so evaluate(arrow) needs one `)` + semicolon: `}));`? Let's parse: `page.evaluate(() => ({ ... }))` — arrow returns parenthesized object, so closing is `}))` then `;`? Actually `() => ({...})` has `(` before `{` and `)` after `}`. Then evaluate's `)` -> total `}))`. Then `;`. So `}));` is correct. Yes.

Wait in test5 I used block body:
