AI/battle banners could block map clicks if pointer-events auto; set them pointer-events none. Side panels need auto. Also maybe `#game` itself should not capture.

Add CSS:
```
#game{pointer-events:none}
#game .side-panel{pointer-events:auto}
#game .ai-banner,#game .battle-banner{pointer-events:none}
```
But side-panel on mobile closed has pointer-events:none via media query, and .open sets auto. Our rule `#game .side-panel{pointer-events:auto}` has specificity (0,1,1) vs `.left-panel` (0,1,0) in media; might override mobile closed pointer-events none! Need avoid. Instead use `#game .side-panel{pointer-events:auto}` only desktop, and mobile media `.side-panel` rule later with `pointer-events:none` but specificity lower (0,1,0) vs (0,1,1) -> loses. So better add a class or use `#game .side-panel:not(.open)`? Hmm.

Simpler: set `#game{pointer-events:none}` and then add `pointer-events:auto` to `.side-panel` in base CSS (line 143), and in mobile media `.side-panel` already sets pointer-events:none for closed, `.open` auto. Since `.side-panel` base and media same specificity, later media wins. Good. Similarly `.hud` already none with children auto, `.bottom-bar` none with children auto. So just add `pointer-events:auto` to `.side-panel` base and `#game{pointer-events:none}`.

But #game pointer-events none also affects modal? Modal layer is likely outside #game? Check index around modal.

